
For the purposes of electing the Presidency Ranked Voting1 shall proceed
as follows:
(i) A  list  of  valid  nominations,  in  alphabetical  order,  will  be
provided  on a  secret  ballot  to each  Financial Member
present at the election.

(ii) Each Financial Member eligible to vote shall:
1. rank each nominee from one (1) to “x” where x =
the total number of nominees. One (1) shall
represent a preference for the nominee to take the
highest position in leadership (typically the
President), and x represents the lowest (typically a
Vice President); or
2. vote under the category of “no vote”, where there
shall be no ranking presented for any candidate.

(iii) Notwithstanding a “no vote”, each rank must be filled by a
single nominee.
(iv) At  the  conclusion  of  voting  each  nominee  shall  have  their
ranks tallied. For example, if nominee y received from one
Member a rank of 2 out of 4, and from  another Member a
rank of 1 out of 4, their overall score shall be 3 plus the ranks
given  by  all  other  Members.  The  three  nominees  with  the
lowest overall scores shall be provisionally nominated to the
Presidency and begin discussions following clause 9.5(f)(ii).
(v) In a vote by a member of the (Outgoing) Executive, each numerical rank shall first
be multiplied by two and then tallied in order to count as two votes.